{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_grdh7xgph6ok254tapi46xdqkxvfy3vkzigfx3yewdbvn6mqdfia","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Here's the summary:\n\n## What the code is\n\n`c_src/` is stb_perlin.h (Perlin noise, 7 functions) plus a `main.c` driver that `scanf`s 12 values and `printf(\"%.9g\")`s one result. The Rust side had **no library target at all**, so nothing was exported.\n\n## Phase A — surface artifacts (in crate root)\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | 9 C dynamic symbols → all 9 now exported by the Rust `.so`, 0 undefined non-libc symbols. Documents the observed `.data` layout (`randtab`+512→`grad_idx`+1024→`basis`) that the OOB model depends on. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 44 `E` rows + 9 `G` rows, grepped from the C: the library has **no** error codes/asserts/null checks — `inner`'s `default: return NAN` is the only sentinel; everything else is a degenerate or UB path, each with the measured C result. |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 53 `C` rows (wrap options × seed shapes × coordinate shapes × fractal params × `which` × driver input shapes) + 4 build-config rows. |\n\n## Two real divergences found and fixed (C never touched)\n\n1. **NaN sign/payload propagation** — x86 `addss/subss/mulss` return the *destination* operand's NaN; gcc's operand order (read from `objdump -d`) differs from LLVM's in `lerp` (`a + (b-a)*t` → the product is dest) and `grad` (`g2*z` is dest of the 2nd add, so `z`'s NaN outranks `x`'s). User-visible: `0 nan 1 -nan …` printed `nan` in Rust vs **`-nan`** in C. Fixed with explicit `sse_add/sse_sub/sse_mul` helpers.\n2. **`scanf(\"%f\")` hex floats** — glibc *accepts* `0x.`, `0x.p1`, `0x.g` (value `0`, and must not eat the `p`), rejecting only a bare `0x`. Rust rejected them: `1 0x. 2.25 …` gave `0.111367986` in C vs `0` in Rust. Reimplemented glibc's collector state machine, plus single-rounding (sticky bit) for the hex mantissa.\n\n## Test infrastructure (89 tests)\n\n- Added `[lib] crate-type = [\"cdylib\",\"rlib\"]` with one `#[no_mangle] extern \"C\"` wrapper per C symbol (incl. `inner` and `main`); tests load **both** `.so`s via `libloading` and compare `f32::to_bits()`.\n- `main` compared three ways: C exe vs Rust bin, and the `main` **export** of both `.so`s via `src/bin/so_main_runner.rs` (dlopen).\n- `cscan`/`cfmt` additionally compared **directly against glibc** (`sscanf`/`snprintf` via FFI): 40 000 random tokens (value + `%n` consumption) and 400 000+ `%.9g` values.\n- UB is handled honestly: a classifier splits `wrap_nonpow2` inputs into the reproducible 1024-byte window (bit-exact, 72 000+ comparisons) and genuine UB, where the test *proves* the C exe and C `.so` disagree with each other, and that `INT_MIN % -1` kills C with `SIGFPE`.\n\n## Gate\n\n- ✅ `nm -D` parity, 0 missing / 0 undefined non-libc (debug **and** release)\n- ✅ all 53 `CONFIGS.md` rows, all 44+9 `ERRORS.md` rows pass\n- ✅ 89 tests pass under `--no-default-features`, `--all-features`, default (the crate declares no `[features]`) and `--release`; clean-slate `cargo test` bootstraps every artifact\n- ✅ extra sweep: 1.07M library calls + 2 500 driver inputs, **0 divergences**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":838,"cache_read_input_tokens":395981,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":838,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eab2f7b9-57d5-4ef1-afe3-e4bea75ae637","uuid":"cf3daf0e-abb5-4997-bd5c-1d589e35c0f2","timestamp":"2026-08-19T10:18:13.980Z"}
